<article class="env-lemma" id="03RB">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/03RB">Lemma <span data-tag="03RB">59.67.7</span>.</a> Let $k$ be an algebraically closed field. Let $f_1, \ldots , f_ s \in k[T_1, \ldots , T_ n]$ be homogeneous polynomials of degree $d_1, \ldots , d_ s$ with $d_ i > 0$. If $s < n$, then $f_1 = \ldots = f_ s = 0$ have a common nontrivial solution. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This follows from dimension theory, for example in the form of Varieties, Lemma <a href="/tag/0B2Q" data-tag="0B2Q">33.34.2</a> applied $s - 1$ times. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>